course: dictionary
lesson: 6472
title: Meet the natterjack
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may not know the word natterjack, but the sentence gives you clues. «Male frogs and toads call to attract partners» tells you that frogs and toads are the animals being talked about, and natterjack toads appear in that same list. So a natterjack is a kind of toad.
explain: Look at the next clues: «puff up a vocal sac like a balloon to make the call louder» and «heard over a kilometre away». These tell you that a natterjack's call is very loud, which matches the dictionary entry.
explain: Clues can also work by contrast. «Common frogs purr quietly» sets a quiet sound against the loud calls of natterjack toads. Always ask: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: A natterjack is a small toad found in Europe, including Britain and Ireland.
fact: It has a yellow stripe down its back.
fact: A natterjack runs rather than hops.
fact: Male natterjacks have a very loud croak, which can be heard from far away.
fact: Natterjacks live in sand dunes, heaths and salt marshes, and they are protected in the UK and Ireland.
exercise: In this lesson, what is a natterjack? | A large fish that lives in the sea | A type of frog that purrs quietly | *A small toad with a yellow stripe down its back | A kind of bird that sings at night
exercise: «A natterjack runs rather than hops.» What does this tell you about how it moves? | It hops like a kangaroo | It flies high over the water | *It moves by running along the ground | It can only swim
exercise: Where do natterjacks live? | *Sand dunes, heaths and salt marshes | In the tops of the highest trees | Deep in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean | Inside tall city buildings
test: «The natterjack has a very loud croak.» What does loud mean here? | Slow and gentle | *Easy to hear from far away | Yellow in colour | Soft and quiet
test: «Natterjacks are protected in the UK and Ireland.» What does protected mean? | *Kept safe, because they need help | Sold in shops | Shouted at by people | Eaten for dinner
exam: Which clue in the example sentence tells you that a natterjack's call can travel a long way? | Male frogs and toads call to attract partners | *Natterjack toads are reported to be heard over a kilometre away | Common frogs purr quietly | Many puff up a vocal sac like a balloon
